values ('ap_precalculus', 2, '2.7', array['2.7']::text[], 'list_sequence', 'Building and decomposing compositions', 'How the CED has students construct a composition and rewrite a function as a composition.', '[{"label": "Analytic construction", "meaning": "Substitute g(x) for every instance of x in f to get f(g(x))."}, {"label": "Numerical or graphical construction", "meaning": "Calculate or estimate values for (x, f(g(x)))."}, {"label": "Decomposition", "meaning": "Break an analytic function into less complicated functions, where the variable in one function replaces each instance of the function it was composed with."}, {"label": "Additive transformation", "meaning": "Vertical and horizontal translations are the composition of g(x) = x + k with f."}, {"label": "Multiplicative transformation", "meaning": "Vertical and horizontal dilations are the composition of g(x) = kx with f."}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-precalculus-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_precalculus-u2-r2-009; ced=2.7.B.2 "substituting g(x) for every instance of x in f"; 2.7.C.2 and 2.7.C.3 "composition of g(x) = x + k with f" / "g(x) = kx with f"')
